{"status":"completed","summary":"Repaired node1’s status writer. SIGHUP now reloads valid configuration in the same process, empty configuration is rejected while retaining the last valid message, SIGTERM exits cleanly, and exactly one writer persists across reboot. Existing journal entries, RHEL release, and kernel were preserved.","actions_performed":["Replaced worker.py with Python 3.12-compatible signal handling and a singleton file lock.","Added and enabled a hardened systemd service with reload support and failure recovery.","Verified valid reload, empty-config rejection, clean SIGTERM shutdown, and single-writer operation.","Restored message.conf to its original value and removed temporary test artifacts.","Restarted node1 once and verified boot identity change, service recovery, journal continuity, and post-restart reload behavior."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"SIGHUP reloads message.conf without terminating the process or creating another writer","command_ids":["cmd-e13391668241465f"],"summary":"PID remained 2028, exact writer count remained one, and the reloaded message appeared in journal.txt."},{"requirement":"Empty configuration is rejected while retaining the last valid message","command_ids":["cmd-3c416f4fe5674dbb"],"summary":"The rejection was logged, PID remained unchanged, writer count stayed one, no blank journal lines appeared, and the prior valid message continued."},{"requirement":"SIGTERM exits cleanly","command_ids":["cmd-3f23d57e02e64c04"],"summary":"The service exited successfully with status 0, writer count became zero, and journal growth stopped."},{"requirement":"Original configuration and journal history are preserved","command_ids":["cmd-c12afb43811444be","cmd-69e8180544564538","cmd-976befc2224544e2"],"summary":"message.conf was restored to “branch status: open”; the historical first entry remains “branch status: opening”; writing continues normally."},{"requirement":"Writer is enabled, active, and single-instance","command_ids":["cmd-69e8180544564538","cmd-976befc2224544e2"],"summary":"The service is enabled and active with exactly one worker process before and after restart."},{"requirement":"Installed operating-system release and kernel were retained","command_ids":["cmd-f382cc2e07b24ac7","cmd-976befc2224544e2"],"summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 remained unchanged."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-3b07029312224362","cmd-51692cd4944a46cc","cmd-4a64f87442624f17","cmd-976befc2224544e2"],"summary":"Healthy baseline captured; reboot acknowledged; boot ID changed from 646e5f74-dc0e-45e7-9746-226c4351af28 to b91ff222-d023-4c64-834d-a7d1325f273b; system, service, single-writer state, configuration, journal data, and SIGHUP reload all recovered."}]}
